invariant: INV-16
file: sha512_compress_blocks.c
catches: test/lint-wide-multiply.sh
reason: next_word writes a schedule word to the ring only where it differs
  from the word it replaces, so whether W[t] equals W[t - 16] decides
  which path runs, and under HMAC-SHA-384 both are computed from the key.
  The value is the same and every digest is right. The multiply tokens
  see nothing. The branch count does: the arm64 and the x86-64 spec each
  emit more conditional branches in sha512_compress_blocks.c than the
  three its ceiling records, which are the test for no block and the two
  loops.

--- old
    ring[i] = word;
    return word;
--- new
    if (word != kept(&ring[i])) {
        ring[i] = word;
    }
    return word;
